<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/vulnerabilityExploitabilityAssessment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A reference to a Vulnerability Exploitability eXchange (VEX) statement which provides information on whether a product is impacted by a specific vulnerability in an included package and, if affected, whether there are actions recommended to remediate. See also [NTIA VEX one-page summary](https://ntia.gov/files/ntia/publications/vex_one-page_summary.pdf)."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/SbomType/deployed> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SBOM provides an inventory of software that is present on a system. This may be an assembly of other SBOMs that combines analysis of configuration options, and examination of execution behavior in a (potentially simulated) deployment environment."@en .
